          "targetDoi": "10.3389/fnrgo.2024.1345507",
          "snippet": "With the method of our protocol (i.e., the use of the Eye Tracker), it was not possible to study the number of blinks because during the MATB, subjects frequently look at the keyword, and therefore, the signal is lost. Nevertheless, in future studies, the use of EOG to assess blinks would improve the overall multimodal physiological characteristics for monitoring mental workload [  54  ]. In our study, the Z-score for the amplitude in the pupil dilation response correlated negatively with the RMSD measure of MATB tracking performance in all four experimental conditions (i.e., the higher RMSD measure, indicating poor tracking performance).",
