        {
          "sourceDoi": "10.3390/clockssleep6030024",
          "targetDoi": "10.1016/0165-1781(89)90047-4",
          "snippet": "We included seventeen healthy men (20–45 years) with no history of contraindication to altitude exposure or high-altitude exposure in the past 3 months. We excluded subjects with sleep disturbances, verified by the Pittsburg sleep quality index &gt;5 [  61  ] or a usual TST &lt; 6 h. The protocol was approved by the “Comité de protection des personnes (CPP) Ile de France VIII”, national IDRCB n°2022-A00464-39. All procedures were conducted in accordance with the Declaration of Helsinki, as revised in 2001.",
